1
00:00:08,559 --> 00:00:11,687
[WILLIAM] This class system
is a curse on civilization.

2
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:15,524
It causes people's hearts to
become poisoned and twisted.

3
00:00:15,566 --> 00:00:19,152
As a result,
it gives rise to devils.

4
00:00:19,194 --> 00:00:22,531
Therefore, the opposite
must also be true.

5
00:00:22,573 --> 00:00:26,159
Once the demon is exorcised,
the heart can become pure.

6
00:00:26,201 --> 00:00:28,203
And the curse, lifted.

7
00:00:28,245 --> 00:00:32,583
Mark my words, this
country will be purified.

8
00:00:34,251 --> 00:00:38,422
[WILLIAM] Are you going to
report me to Scotland yard?

9
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:42,509
As a nobleman,
I bet you'd like that--

10
00:00:42,551 --> 00:00:45,429
to see me taken
away in shackles.

11
00:00:50,601 --> 00:00:51,811
[ALBERT]
An orphan,

12
00:00:51,852 --> 00:00:55,481
with the intellect to leave
even adults speechless.

13
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:59,485
Initially, I simply regarded
him as some sort of prodigy.

14
00:00:59,526 --> 00:01:01,236
That was all.

15
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:04,030
Nothing else
triggered my interest.

16
00:01:04,072 --> 00:01:07,326
But that soon changed.

17
00:01:10,245 --> 00:01:12,790
Please come and live with me.

18
00:03:11,784 --> 00:03:15,454
[SIMON]
Welcome home, Mister Albert.

19
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:16,538
Hold it right there.

20
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:18,665
[BOTH grunt]

21
00:03:18,707 --> 00:03:20,834
You may be Mister
Albert's guests,

22
00:03:20,876 --> 00:03:24,212
but I can't let you track
your filth into the foyer.

23
00:03:24,254 --> 00:03:26,506
Go in through the back.

24
00:03:29,175 --> 00:03:30,928
[ALBERT]
Simon!

25
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:32,137
Step back.

26
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:34,765
Those aren't just my guests
that you're insulting.

27
00:03:34,807 --> 00:03:38,477
They're the newest
members of my family.

28
00:03:38,518 --> 00:03:39,770
[SIMON grunts]

29
00:03:42,397 --> 00:03:44,942
I don't understand.
What's the meaning of this?

30
00:03:44,984 --> 00:03:47,694
I did tell you that we'd
be taking in an orphan.

31
00:03:47,736 --> 00:03:49,488
[COUNTESS MORIARTY]
Yes, an orphan.

32
00:03:49,529 --> 00:03:51,323
So why are there two of them?!

33
00:03:51,364 --> 00:03:53,408
[EARL MORIARTY]
That was Albert's decision.

34
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:55,494
[COUNTESS MORIARTY] Well, why
don't you make him "decide"

35
00:03:55,535 --> 00:03:57,203
which one he wants to keep?

36
00:03:57,245 --> 00:03:58,831
[WILLIAM]
Shouldn't be a hard choice.

37
00:03:58,872 --> 00:04:00,916
I hear the younger
one's quite ill.

38
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:03,209
We may as well be
adopting plague rats.

39
00:04:03,251 --> 00:04:04,878
[COUNTESS MORIARTY] William has
the right of it, Darling.

40
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:07,923
What if these urchins get one
of our children sick?

41
00:04:07,965 --> 00:04:09,133
[EARL MORIARTY]
This discussion is over.

42
00:04:09,174 --> 00:04:11,468
The plague rats stay.

43
00:04:13,971 --> 00:04:16,348
[DUCHESS PÉNIÈRES]
My goodness. Lord Moriarty.

44
00:04:16,389 --> 00:04:19,309
I can't believe you've
adopted two orphans.

45
00:04:19,351 --> 00:04:21,020
Well, I couldn't
just take in one.

46
00:04:21,061 --> 00:04:23,271
They're brothers after all.

47
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:26,817
[EARL MORIARTY]
I've always felt it a duty

48
00:04:26,859 --> 00:04:28,152
of those of us who have,

49
00:04:28,193 --> 00:04:31,530
to extend a hand
to those who have not.

50
00:04:31,571 --> 00:04:33,866
I hear that the younger
brother is quite ill,

51
00:04:33,907 --> 00:04:36,118
but you're providing
for his treatment.

52
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,828
[EARL MORIARTY]
Indeed I am.

53
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:40,873
The doctor tells me the boy's
condition is quite serious.

54
00:04:40,914 --> 00:04:44,043
The product of a lifetime
of hardships, no doubt.

55
00:04:44,084 --> 00:04:46,920
That said, if all goes well
with the operation,

56
00:04:46,962 --> 00:04:49,631
I'll make sure he
has a bright future.

57
00:04:49,673 --> 00:04:52,467
[gasps] Oh!

58
00:05:07,858 --> 00:05:09,026
[LOUIS groans]

59
00:05:09,068 --> 00:05:11,236
[WILLIAM grunts]

60
00:05:11,277 --> 00:05:13,906
[LOUIS groaning]

61
00:05:13,947 --> 00:05:15,407
No, not again!

62
00:05:15,448 --> 00:05:16,366
This is bad.

63
00:05:16,408 --> 00:05:18,160
Just hold on,
I'll be back with help.

64
00:05:18,202 --> 00:05:23,331
[LOUIS] No, wait, don't leave.
Please, just stay here.

65
00:05:23,373 --> 00:05:25,458
I know how this
looks but I'm fine.

66
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,710
Trust me.

67
00:05:26,752 --> 00:05:31,840
This'll be over before long.
I just need you with me.

68
00:05:31,882 --> 00:05:33,633
That's all.

69
00:05:48,899 --> 00:05:50,943
[WILLIAM]
You there!

70
00:05:50,984 --> 00:05:53,779
I'm parched, why don't
you make me some tea?

71
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:57,490
Well, all right.
As you wish, Master William.

72
00:06:07,251 --> 00:06:09,544
[LOUIS]
Is this all right?

73
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,602
No, it's not.

74
00:06:27,395 --> 00:06:28,605
[LOUIS gasps]

75
00:06:30,315 --> 00:06:32,234
[WILLIAM] We can muck
the grime from your skin

76
00:06:32,276 --> 00:06:33,902
but not your mind, it seems.

77
00:06:33,944 --> 00:06:35,821
What possessed you
to think I'd drink tea

78
00:06:35,862 --> 00:06:38,448
made by a worthless
wretch like you?

79
00:06:38,490 --> 00:06:39,950
What a mess you've made.

80
00:06:39,992 --> 00:06:42,619
Albert didn't tell us you
weren't house-trained.

81
00:06:42,661 --> 00:06:47,124
Come fix what you've done.
Clean it up with your tongue.

82
00:06:52,171 --> 00:06:55,132
[WILLIAM]
Might I clean it in his place?

83
00:06:55,174 --> 00:06:56,382
[LOUIS gasps]

84
00:06:58,051 --> 00:06:59,719
[LOUIS]
Brother.

85
00:06:59,761 --> 00:07:03,431
[chuckles] Trying to protect
your younger brother

86
00:07:03,473 --> 00:07:05,267
from his own carelessness?

87
00:07:05,309 --> 00:07:08,270
Familial love is
a beautiful thing.

88
00:07:08,312 --> 00:07:11,397
I'm surprised that your kind
is capable of such a feeling.

89
00:07:11,439 --> 00:07:14,151
Thought it would be
too complex for you.

90
00:07:14,193 --> 00:07:17,403
However, if you truly wish
to be of help to your brother,

91
00:07:17,445 --> 00:07:18,613
I should like you to teach him

92
00:07:18,655 --> 00:07:21,741
that his actions
have consequences.

93
00:07:21,783 --> 00:07:24,619
And naturally, since
you two are of a baser class,

94
00:07:24,661 --> 00:07:27,455
you have a hard time learning
through conventional means.

95
00:07:27,497 --> 00:07:29,457
So, drive the lesson
home with this.

96
00:07:29,499 --> 00:07:31,960
Engrave it, lest he forgets.

97
00:07:53,106 --> 00:07:55,025
[ALL gasping]

98
00:08:06,161 --> 00:08:08,705
Does seeing this
make you feel better?

99
00:08:12,709 --> 00:08:14,627
[ALBERT]
I'm sorry.

100
00:08:14,669 --> 00:08:17,756
I wanted to offer you
a home, but not this.

101
00:08:17,797 --> 00:08:19,925
We're in your debt
even now, my lord.

102
00:08:19,966 --> 00:08:21,009
You've done nothing wrong,

103
00:08:21,051 --> 00:08:23,720
so don't concern yourself
with our troubles.

104
00:08:23,762 --> 00:08:26,681
You should go--your father
doesn't want you visiting.

105
00:08:26,723 --> 00:08:29,517
I think he's afraid that
we'll taint you somehow.

106
00:08:29,559 --> 00:08:30,269
I--

107
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:32,478
[WILLIAM]
Please, let it be.

108
00:08:47,202 --> 00:08:48,536
[WILLIAM]
What's wrong?

109
00:08:50,038 --> 00:08:52,498
[LOUIS]
Nothing.

110
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,584
I guess I was just wondering.

111
00:08:54,626 --> 00:08:57,963
Why do you think Mister Albert
invited us to live here?

112
00:08:58,004 --> 00:09:00,548
Was it out of sympathy
for my illness?

113
00:09:00,590 --> 00:09:04,469
Or a sense of aristocratic
obligation, maybe?

114
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:07,680
Despite his family, he's
been truly helpful to us.

115
00:09:07,722 --> 00:09:09,724
But we're penniless orphans.

116
00:09:09,766 --> 00:09:12,978
So I can't see how he expects
us to repay his kindness.

117
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:15,188
Or if he even does.

118
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:18,317
[WILLIAM] People use each
other without exception.

119
00:09:18,358 --> 00:09:20,568
It's the principle
of mutual aid.

120
00:09:20,610 --> 00:09:23,238
I don't consider it
such a bad thing.

121
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,573
He'll use us as we've used him.

122
00:09:25,615 --> 00:09:28,660
After all, his offer
was quite generous.

123
00:09:31,163 --> 00:09:33,206
For now, let's watch and wait.

124
00:09:33,248 --> 00:09:34,958
He'll approach us soon.

125
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,627
And tell us what
he wants himself.

126
00:09:37,669 --> 00:09:39,796
Though if this
were a horse race,

127
00:09:39,838 --> 00:09:42,882
I'd be ready to
place my bet now.

128
00:09:53,393 --> 00:09:54,436
[COUNTESS MORIARTY]
William.

129
00:09:54,478 --> 00:09:56,729
You're due to attend
classes at Eton College

130
00:09:56,771 --> 00:09:58,482
before too long, aren't you?

131
00:09:58,523 --> 00:10:00,984
I do wish you'd commit
to your studies more.

132
00:10:02,777 --> 00:10:04,821
I would, but I
can't concentrate.

133
00:10:04,863 --> 00:10:07,449
Not while you're raising
those low-born parasites

134
00:10:07,491 --> 00:10:08,700
under our roof.

135
00:10:08,741 --> 00:10:10,160
There's no telling
what they might do

136
00:10:10,202 --> 00:10:13,788
if I lower my guard around them.

137
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:17,167
Well? What do you think?
Can we end this farce yet?

138
00:10:17,209 --> 00:10:19,711
Frankly, we should've run
those two off a while ago.

139
00:10:19,752 --> 00:10:22,130
We cured the younger
one's illness, haven't we?

140
00:10:22,172 --> 00:10:24,549
That's enough to
save appearances.

141
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,259
That doesn't even come close.

142
00:10:26,301 --> 00:10:29,262
If we dismiss them,
the gossip will be insufferable.

143
00:10:29,304 --> 00:10:33,099
And I'll be the one who has
to suffer the brunt of it.

144
00:10:33,141 --> 00:10:35,977
If only one of them
would commit some sort of crime.

145
00:10:36,019 --> 00:10:38,771
Then we could be rid
of them without a fuss.

146
00:10:46,238 --> 00:10:48,281
[EARL MORIARTY]
Incidentally, William.

147
00:10:48,323 --> 00:10:50,867
As I was boarding my
carriage in town yesterday,

148
00:10:50,909 --> 00:10:53,828
some street peddler
offered me his thanks.

149
00:10:53,870 --> 00:10:56,664
He made it sound like you'd done
some sort of favour for him.

150
00:10:56,706 --> 00:10:59,376
Well, that's odd.
He must've had the wrong person.

151
00:10:59,418 --> 00:11:01,461
You would never
catch me wasting my time

152
00:11:01,503 --> 00:11:03,422
talking to a street peddler.

153
00:11:03,463 --> 00:11:06,758
Honestly, they're only
a half-step up from beggars.

154
00:11:06,799 --> 00:11:10,387
They certainly have the same
smell of sweat and piss.

155
00:11:10,429 --> 00:11:12,013
Well, you can't argue with that.

156
00:11:12,055 --> 00:11:14,224
Don't encourage him
to say such filth.

157
00:11:14,266 --> 00:11:17,185
At least not during
our meals. It's unseemly.

158
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:18,978
[WILLIAM]
Fine, forget the urchins.

159
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:22,148
Oh! My birthday will be the
same day as Easter this year,

160
00:11:22,190 --> 00:11:24,817
so my party needs
to be larger than usual.

161
00:11:24,859 --> 00:11:26,319
Can I invite anyone?

162
00:11:26,361 --> 00:11:27,320
[EARL MORIARTY]
None of the children

163
00:11:27,362 --> 00:11:29,489
from Baron Kimble's family.

164
00:11:29,531 --> 00:11:32,033
I'm told that they've run into
financial trouble as of late.

165
00:11:32,075 --> 00:11:33,285
[WILLIAM]
Right.

166
00:11:33,326 --> 00:11:35,870
He's just a life peer anyway,
so they won't inherit.

167
00:11:35,912 --> 00:11:36,996
[COUNTESS MORIARTY]
Be sure that the son of the

168
00:11:37,038 --> 00:11:38,831
Marquess of Lytton attends.

169
00:11:38,873 --> 00:11:40,208
[clattering]

170
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:41,626
[BOTH grunt]

171
00:11:43,753 --> 00:11:46,005
Is everything all right
with you, Albert?

172
00:11:46,047 --> 00:11:48,341
You've been acting rather
strange as of late.

173
00:11:48,383 --> 00:11:51,261
[ALBERT]
You're the ones who are strange.

174
00:11:51,303 --> 00:11:52,804
[COUNTESS MORIARTY gasps]
Wait, Albert!

175
00:11:52,845 --> 00:11:53,721
Come back!

176
00:11:53,763 --> 00:11:55,599
[ALBERT]
I don't want to talk to you.

177
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,183
Or hear your voices.

178
00:11:57,225 --> 00:12:00,019
Or look at your faces.

179
00:12:00,061 --> 00:12:03,189
All that power.
All that privilege.

180
00:12:03,231 --> 00:12:07,277
And you wield it only
to push others down.

181
00:12:07,319 --> 00:12:09,446
You're befouling this world.

182
00:12:09,488 --> 00:12:12,157
And I can't stop you.

183
00:12:18,497 --> 00:12:22,626
[ALBERT] The world as
I know it is driven by "status."

184
00:12:22,667 --> 00:12:25,920
Everyone covets it.
Hoards what they can.

185
00:12:25,962 --> 00:12:28,798
And feign like they have more.

186
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,259
It makes us look up
at some in envy

187
00:12:31,301 --> 00:12:33,845
and down at the rest in scorn.

188
00:12:36,806 --> 00:12:40,018
[ALBERT] Why is this
family--this world

189
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:42,228
so horrifically cruel?

190
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:43,938
So twisted?

191
00:12:45,482 --> 00:12:47,400
[ALBERT]
Do you have the answer?

192
00:12:47,442 --> 00:12:50,111
These people are poison.

193
00:12:50,153 --> 00:12:54,324
They taint the very
air they breathe.

194
00:12:54,366 --> 00:12:56,576
Am I wrong?

195
00:12:59,996 --> 00:13:01,289
I don't think so.

196
00:13:01,331 --> 00:13:03,749
Is this how you'd like me to
make good on my debt to you?

197
00:13:28,066 --> 00:13:30,694
[EARL MORIARTY snores]

198
00:13:55,552 --> 00:13:57,345
[WILLIAM chuckles]

199
00:13:57,387 --> 00:13:58,430
[WILLIAM]
How convenient.

200
00:13:58,471 --> 00:13:59,764
[gasps]

201
00:14:03,268 --> 00:14:06,479
Wait! I thought I saw
you asleep in your bed.

202
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:08,981
[gasps]

203
00:14:09,023 --> 00:14:10,442
[WILLIAM]
This is perfect.

204
00:14:10,483 --> 00:14:13,445
You've saved me the trouble of
having to move your body later.

205
00:14:13,486 --> 00:14:16,030
Hold on. What are
you talking about?

206
00:14:16,072 --> 00:14:17,616
[WILLIAM]
I see now.

207
00:14:17,657 --> 00:14:19,992
You thought you'd hide
that silverware in our room

208
00:14:20,034 --> 00:14:21,745
and then "discover it" later.

209
00:14:21,786 --> 00:14:25,039
That way you could frame us as
thieves and have us thrown out.

210
00:14:25,081 --> 00:14:26,832
I've heard worse plans.

211
00:14:26,874 --> 00:14:28,126
[grunts]

212
00:14:33,757 --> 00:14:35,174
[yelps]

213
00:14:40,096 --> 00:14:42,974
[WILLIAM] Wait. Just what
are you planning to do?

214
00:14:43,015 --> 00:14:45,226
Murder me?

215
00:14:45,268 --> 00:14:48,187
No. There's someone else
who wants to deal with you.

216
00:14:48,229 --> 00:14:49,689
Huh?

217
00:14:55,153 --> 00:14:56,696
[WILLIAM]
Brother?

218
00:14:56,738 --> 00:14:58,323
You wouldn't.

219
00:15:06,831 --> 00:15:08,500
[ALBERT]
Am I wrong

220
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:10,918
to want to kill for my ideals?

221
00:15:12,878 --> 00:15:14,172
I don't think so.

222
00:15:14,213 --> 00:15:17,091
Is this how you'd like me to
make good on my debt to you?

223
00:15:17,133 --> 00:15:19,469
[ALBERT]
Yes, it is. I need your help.

224
00:15:19,511 --> 00:15:23,848
Give me the wisdom and courage
to achieve my ambitions.

225
00:15:23,889 --> 00:15:25,558
Wisdom I can give.

226
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,977
I'm a consultant
of sorts, after all.

227
00:15:29,061 --> 00:15:32,023
That said, you shouldn't
look to me for courage.

228
00:15:34,567 --> 00:15:37,195
[WILLIAM]
Look to yourself.

229
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:38,363
[WILLIAM]
Albert, please.

230
00:15:38,404 --> 00:15:40,406
How can you even consider this?

231
00:15:40,448 --> 00:15:44,703
Nice to see that you'd
strike first if you could.

232
00:15:44,744 --> 00:15:46,538
[gasps, chuckles] Oh, please.

233
00:15:46,579 --> 00:15:48,414
What damage could
a little fork do?

234
00:15:48,456 --> 00:15:50,792
I would never
hurt you; we're family.

235
00:15:50,834 --> 00:15:53,545
Come on. We share
the same blood. So--

236
00:15:53,586 --> 00:15:55,004
[ALBERT]
Shut your mouth.

237
00:15:55,046 --> 00:15:57,131
The mere idea
the same tainted blood

238
00:15:57,173 --> 00:15:58,800
flows through both of our veins

239
00:15:58,842 --> 00:16:01,927
is enough to make
me want to vomit.

240
00:16:01,969 --> 00:16:03,513
I hold you,

241
00:16:03,555 --> 00:16:04,972
this family,

242
00:16:05,014 --> 00:16:07,975
this whole society in contempt!

243
00:16:08,017 --> 00:16:10,102
I've resolved to change it.

244
00:16:10,144 --> 00:16:12,605
And that starts tonight.

245
00:16:12,647 --> 00:16:13,565
The world I make

246
00:16:13,606 --> 00:16:16,735
will have no place
for people like you.

247
00:16:16,776 --> 00:16:19,320
- -So, die.
- -[WILLIAM groans]

248
00:16:22,365 --> 00:16:25,785
[WILLIAM groans, whimpers]

249
00:16:34,669 --> 00:16:37,171
[panting]

250
00:16:38,673 --> 00:16:40,592
[WILLIAM]
Thank you, Albert.

251
00:16:43,469 --> 00:16:46,681
You've demonstrated
the strength of your resolve.

252
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:53,605
[WILLIAM]
If you pull that out now,

253
00:16:53,646 --> 00:16:56,065
you'll die of rapid blood loss.

254
00:16:56,107 --> 00:16:57,650
It's not essential, but

255
00:16:57,692 --> 00:17:00,986
I'd prefer it if you drew
breath a while longer.

256
00:17:01,028 --> 00:17:01,905
In the unlikely event of

257
00:17:01,946 --> 00:17:04,198
a coroner's inquest
on your corpse,

258
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:07,159
I'd prefer what's left of your
lungs to have internal burns

259
00:17:07,201 --> 00:17:09,788
from inhalation
of searing hot smoke.

260
00:17:09,829 --> 00:17:12,665
[gasps] You... can't.

261
00:17:12,707 --> 00:17:14,876
[WILLIAM]
Hm.

262
00:17:14,918 --> 00:17:17,545
Come. We need to
finish what we've started,

263
00:17:17,587 --> 00:17:18,797
quickly.

264
00:17:20,298 --> 00:17:21,591
[WILLIAM]
In the wake of it all,

265
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:23,217
we want the thought of foul play

266
00:17:23,259 --> 00:17:25,762
to be far from
any onlooker's minds.

267
00:17:25,804 --> 00:17:28,389
If we make this look
like a tragic accident,

268
00:17:28,431 --> 00:17:30,767
we can prevent an investigation.

269
00:17:31,601 --> 00:17:33,561
[WILLIAM]
This is the blueprint

270
00:17:33,603 --> 00:17:36,773
of what you'd call
a perfect crime.

271
00:17:36,815 --> 00:17:38,900
One sure-fire way
to dispose of evidence

272
00:17:38,942 --> 00:17:41,736
is to burn your
crime scene to ash.

273
00:17:41,778 --> 00:17:44,530
Normally, it would be quite
the challenge to burn down

274
00:17:44,572 --> 00:17:46,616
an entire manor of this size.

275
00:17:46,658 --> 00:17:49,452
We'll do it by causing
a major gas leak.

276
00:17:49,494 --> 00:17:52,413
Gas lighting is exceedingly
common these days.

277
00:17:52,455 --> 00:17:54,624
Naturally, we get
the occasional leak.

278
00:17:54,666 --> 00:17:57,126
And the occasional fire.

279
00:17:57,168 --> 00:18:00,588
Thus, there's an extremely
high probability that this

280
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:04,008
will be considered nothing
more than a tragic accident.

281
00:18:06,970 --> 00:18:08,847
This cellar should
be relatively airtight.

282
00:18:08,888 --> 00:18:11,516
So, we'll be safe from
the initial blast at least.

283
00:18:13,601 --> 00:18:15,937
[WILLIAM] There's nothing
left to do now but wait.

284
00:18:15,979 --> 00:18:18,523
The manor's filling
with gas as we speak.

285
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:31,243
[gasping]

286
00:18:56,352 --> 00:18:57,562
[ALBERT grunts]

287
00:19:04,151 --> 00:19:06,571
Let's go. It's coming down.

288
00:19:09,032 --> 00:19:10,157
[LOUIS grunts]

289
00:19:11,993 --> 00:19:13,369
What're you doing?

290
00:19:14,871 --> 00:19:16,372
[groans]

291
00:19:16,414 --> 00:19:18,041
Louis, don't!

292
00:19:18,082 --> 00:19:19,834
Why would you do that?

293
00:19:19,876 --> 00:19:22,378
'Cause it maximizes our chances.

294
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:23,796
And with all our
futures at stake,

295
00:19:23,838 --> 00:19:26,173
it's a small price to pay.

296
00:19:26,215 --> 00:19:27,926
Had we come out
of this unscathed,

297
00:19:27,967 --> 00:19:29,761
someone might've doubted us.

298
00:19:29,802 --> 00:19:32,805
But this wound makes it
clear that we barely escaped.

299
00:19:32,847 --> 00:19:36,183
Also, I still owe you two
for saving me from my illness.

300
00:19:36,225 --> 00:19:37,435
[WILLIAM gasps]

301
00:19:37,476 --> 00:19:39,812
[LOUIS] Please accept this
as my way of repaying you.

302
00:19:39,854 --> 00:19:42,690
And as proof of my resolve
to stand beside you,

303
00:19:42,732 --> 00:19:45,484
engraved, lest I forget.

304
00:19:47,486 --> 00:19:52,617
[ALBERT] As comrades,
accomplices, and family--

305
00:19:52,658 --> 00:19:55,202
this is how we're going to live.

306
00:19:55,995 --> 00:19:57,789
[WILLIAM]
Once the demon is exorcised,

307
00:19:57,830 --> 00:19:59,415
the heart can become pure.

308
00:19:59,457 --> 00:20:01,084
And the curse, lifted.

309
00:20:01,125 --> 00:20:05,379
Mark my words, this
country will be purified.

310
00:20:08,758 --> 00:20:11,052
Please come and live with me.

311
00:20:11,094 --> 00:20:12,095
[gasps]

312
00:20:12,136 --> 00:20:14,263
[ALBERT] I wish to
combine my noble status

313
00:20:14,305 --> 00:20:16,265
with your brilliant mind.

314
00:20:16,307 --> 00:20:21,228
With my wealth, my privilege,
and my loyalty

315
00:20:21,270 --> 00:20:26,109
you shall have all the tools you
need to realize your ambitions.

316
00:20:26,150 --> 00:20:27,860
Use them as you please

317
00:20:27,902 --> 00:20:31,739
and show me the world
as you wish it to be.

318
00:20:49,882 --> 00:20:51,884
Look! There are survivors!

319
00:20:51,926 --> 00:20:53,511
Doctor! Quickly!

320
00:20:53,552 --> 00:20:56,388
[FIREMAN 2A]
Are you all right?

321
00:20:56,430 --> 00:20:58,641
My name is Albert.

322
00:20:58,683 --> 00:21:01,727
Albert James Moriarty.

323
00:21:02,895 --> 00:21:06,149
[ALBERT]
And these two are my brothers,

324
00:21:06,190 --> 00:21:08,400
William and Louis.

325
00:21:12,655 --> 00:21:15,407
[WILLIAM] After the fire,
we were the last of our family.

326
00:21:15,449 --> 00:21:17,076
Lacking anyone else to turn to,

327
00:21:17,118 --> 00:21:18,619
the three of us
relied on each other

328
00:21:18,661 --> 00:21:20,579
and strove to push forward.

329
00:21:20,621 --> 00:21:22,623
That sounds absolutely dreadful.

330
00:21:22,665 --> 00:21:26,210
I'm so sorry for dredging up
such unpleasant memories.

331
00:21:26,251 --> 00:21:27,336
That said, it sounds like

332
00:21:27,378 --> 00:21:30,381
you got to grow up in
a truly warm household.

333
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:32,800
A stately father,
a loving mother,

334
00:21:32,842 --> 00:21:34,886
and a quartet of loyal brothers.

335
00:21:34,927 --> 00:21:36,846
It's tragic that you
were torn apart.

336
00:21:36,888 --> 00:21:40,391
But for a time at least,
you had the perfect family.

337
00:21:40,432 --> 00:21:41,976
Yes.

338
00:21:44,269 --> 00:21:45,521
[WILLIAM]
Quite.

339
00:23:34,297 --> 00:23:36,966
[WILLIAM] Next time
on Moriarty the Patriot  .

340
00:23:37,008 --> 00:23:38,425
"A Rare Breed."
